# Line endings are LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# This matters more here than in most repos: tests/fixtures/expected-payload.json is compared
# BYTE FOR BYTE against freshly built JSON (PayloadSnapshotTest). With core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout hands that file back as CRLF, and the comparison fails on a file nobody
# touched. The test currently survives only because it strips \r from the expected side by hand —
# a workaround for a problem that should not exist, and one that protects exactly one fixture.
#
# This changes no blob: everything is already stored LF. It only stops checkout rewriting it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.zip binary
*.mo binary
